<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28836" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĕrŭla</span></b> , ae,
			f. (post-class. collat. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĕrŭlus</span></b> , i,
			m., Auct. Carm. Philom. 13), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a blackbird, ousel, merle</i>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">evolare merulas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fin. 5, 15, 42</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut merula, quia sola volat, quasi mera volans
					nominaretur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 6, 38</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Plin. 10, 29, 42, § 80</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 30, 45, §
			87</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 53, 74,
				§ 147</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A fish, the sea-carp</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">merulae virentes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. Hal.
					114</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Plin. 32, 11, 53, §
			149</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A kind of hydraulic machine that produced a sound
				like the note of the blackbird</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 10,
			12</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
